dren so early  and little kids are very honest so  they'll tell you that so we really have  some work to do in our country with  perceptions starting from our very young  children and believing you know who  could be a scientist who could be a  college graduate you know who could be a  professional  you know we need to do a lot with  perceptions later that day i found  myself with my own little girl  at her parent day at her school and then  i caught a plane to go to phoenix and in  phoenix i went to a policy conference  when i go to a policy conference i'm  usually the only teacher there  i am the  teacher voice  the teacher voice  and in that particular situation at this  particular event we went on a tour of a  vocational school you know we have a lot  of students in our country who are on a  vocational track this is just a fact and  we have to serve their needs we also  have to understand our vocational  students because vocational students  also have college plans i got news for  you and often they have very big goals  and they have it all figured out because  they explain it to me they say yeah i'm  going to graduate from high school i'm  going to get this job i'm going to save  money then i'm going to go to college  then i'm going to go back and start my  own business so  it's very unfair of us  to put people on tracks and say well  you're either vocational or you're  academic because there's so much  crossover so i'd have a chance to go to  that school or chat on educator  effectiveness a little bit of networking  and then finally i was done  giving my own keynote and you might  think about this week that i just  described and somebody asked me once  they said what do you do when you get  sick  it's just not on the schedule it's just  it just doesn't happen you just um  fortunately i've had a very good year  but i've not gotten sick but that  particular week i got to go home on  sunday and you say well that's nice you  get at least you get to get home every 