cher in  training  will step into that room with the  students on the screen  and practice teaching them  before they get in front of live  children  this is new to me  i just saw this last week  i don't know what i think about it  because i'm still trying to reflect and  process it but as i say when i travel  not only am i sharing things from my own  perspective but i'm learning about the  different things that are going on and i  tell you things are really rapidly  changing in education  i was at manhattanville college in  purchase new york talking with teacher  candidates there went to kent state ohio  talked with then i came back to new york  for a stem panel and again this is  another situation where i am the only  teacher on the panel and then a little  bit more with career tech and on to  texas so it gives you an idea of kind of  the schedule and things that people are  talking about i think one of the most  valuable experiences for me this year's  national teacher is to be in close  contact with the business community  and hear about what they want our  students to be able to do and it's a  very different conversation often that  we're having in the education world you  know where we are in education right now  we talk a lot about curriculum and  testing and scores and standards very  interesting to have conversations with  people from the business world who have  a whole different set of expectations  for our students  and sometimes they'll say point blank  you know i don't care if you have a  straight a student who can get fives on  every ap test  if they can't also  step up and take a leadership role  work with self-confidence  be resilient and adaptable and  reflective  and independent and resilient and all  these other factors that they want our  students to be in fact i went to a  science facility in spokane washington  and i point blank asked the researchers  there i said if i could transport you  back to urbana high school to talk with  my students what would you tell them is  the most important thing that they need  to succeed in your scientific facility  and one of the researchers said the  ability to think critically and to  analyze and to reason and one of them  said the ability to solve problems  creatively to work without a manual to  move forward you know even when things  go wrong and then the third said  something very interesting she said your  students need to be able to see beyond  themselves  to see beyond themselves  and that's very interesting perspective  and as we teach and we think about how  we're going to teach all these different  things i mean where where is the app for  that where is the technology that's  going to help me teach my students to  see beyond themselves  but there's all these expectations that  our students are going to have as  finished products when they graduate  from high school when you graduate from  college that people are going to expect  you to be all these things and that  somehow through education we're  providing all of that and it kind of  sums up here in a visual like this  you know as we go about curriculum and  objectives and testing and mastering  material  we also have to be thinking about all  these things in every subject area  literacy and problem solving  communication presentation critical  thinking and i tell you it's that little  blue box self management  that's what people really want  when you graduate from college you  graduate from high school to have all  those interpersonal skills  and you know that's a lot to teach it's  a lot to teach but we're not  having  conversations going on on the other side  of the world had the opportunity to go  to china  met with the director general of  education in china and they're having  some of the same conversations  um specifically they need great teachers  too  because they have a lot of people to  educate and we said well what are you  doing to get great teachers into the  profession and they shared that a 